# A static, spherically symmetric metric with an UNKNOWN radial
# function f(r) in place of a closed form -- Marco 6 step 4
# (DESIGN-M6-PREP.md section 1): represents and derives, never solves.
# f(r) is an indeterminate function, not an alias and not a known
# function (sin/cos/exp/sinh/cosh) -- an opaque symbol the engine never
# evaluates, whose only property is that it has derivatives (f', f''),
# themselves opaque. This is the reciprocal-metric ansatz
# (g_tt = -f(r), g_rr = 1/f(r)) every closed-form static spherical
# solution in this repo's other fixtures (Schwarzschild, Reissner-
# Nordstrom) already specializes -- written here with f(r) left
# unknown, on purpose, to prove the engine carries an indeterminate
# function all the way from the metric through to a real Christoffel
# computation without ever needing to know what f actually is.
manifold M dim 4
bundle TM on M dim 4
chart schw on M coords (t, r, theta, phi)
metric g on schw bundle TM {
  [t,t] = -f(r),
  [r,r] = 1/f(r),
  [theta,theta] = r^2,
  [phi,phi] = r^2 * sin(theta)^2
}
